        "uuid": "ded47fcf_6d81b697",
        "filename": "common/ec_features.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 132,
      "author": {
        "id": 1106949
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-21T20:54:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Then, don\u0027t we need to disable other stuff in motion_lid.c as well? It\u0027s not mandated that a host process checks ec features before getting lid angles. Also, motion_sense_task calls motion_lid_calc wastefully.",
      "parentUuid": "bef8fac1_f3dfac0b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 131,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 132,
        "endChar": 42
      },
      "revId": "ffb4c6631b3404d9f0c93c325c50f999a97c1fab",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a1ec78a9_9ec0a512",
        "filename": "common/ec_features.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 132,
      "author": {
        "id": 1104704
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-28T19:38:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If the attribute `EC_FEATURE_REFINED_TABLET_MODE_HYSTERESIS` is missing, the kernel will not present `cros-ec-lid-angle`, so apps like chrome will calculate the lid angle manually and will not expect a tablet switch. \n\nInternally, motion_lid_calc() will never be called (one sensor is always missing for calculating the lid angle, so the lid angle will always be unreliable. lid_angle_update() is never called.\n\nIn addition, the attribute `kb_wake_angle` won\u0027t be shown either because only one accelerometer is presented.\n\nBeside the code space waste, there is not much runtime waste.",
      "parentUuid": "ded47fcf_6d81b697",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 131,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 132,
        "endChar": 42
      },
      "revId": "ffb4c6631b3404d9f0c93c325c50f999a97c1fab",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
